4, "poll_margin": -0.83, "poll_sd": 4.9, "poll_weight": 0.54, "fundamentals": {"margin": 1.77, "lean": -0.75, "environment": 4.1, "incumbency": 0.0, "money": -1.58}, "rating_margin": 2.33, "sigma_race": 5.5, "sigma_total": 5.95, "baseline_margin": 0.51, "analyst_adjustment": 0.29, "key_factors": ["Polling is a dead heat, with September surveys tilting one to three points toward Jackson", "Prediction markets price Bottoms at 53-56 percent, a modest Democratic edge", "Jackson's massive fundraising advantage against Bottoms's thin cash on hand", "Split expert ratings: four Tossup calls against two Democratic leans"], "rationale": "September polls show a tied race with a slight Republican tilt, but prediction markets and two ratings outlets give Bottoms a modest edge, and this year's political environment leans Democratic. Jackson's fundraising dominance keeps the race genuinely competitive, leaving it near even with a small Democratic lean.", "watch": "The upcoming town hall debate and Medicaid messaging could break the tie, and Jackson's spending advantage may still move the roughly seven percent of undecided voters.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["Open seat: Brian Kemp (R) is not on the ballot."]}, "overview": "Georgia's governor's race is an open-seat contest between Democrat Keisha Lance Bottoms and Republican Rick Jackson, with Republican Brian Kemp term-limited. Polling shows a dead heat: a late-September survey had the candidates tied at 50 percent each, while other September polls put Jackson ahead by one to three points. Averages across outlets span from Jackson plus one to Bottoms plus nearly three, clustering near even.\n\nPrediction markets give Bottoms a 53 to 56 percent chance, and two ratings outlets lean Democratic while four call the race a tossup. Jackson has raised vastly more money than Bottoms, whose cash on hand is thin, making Republican spending a major factor. With a nearly even state lean and an environment that favors Democrats this year, the race sits on a knife's edge.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.6414, "margin": 1.75}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.5561, "margin": 0.5}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.5612, "margin": 0.5}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.5894, "margin": 0.8}]}